  "hints": [
    "In 2D, F = ⟨P, Q⟩ can only be conservative if ∂P/∂y = ∂Q/∂x."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "$\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1$ but $\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 3$.",
    "The cross-partials differ, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative and has no potential function."
  ],
